      'The fix is sequential. A chemical iron remover dissolves the embedded metal first, and you can watch it bleed purple as it works. Clay then shears off whatever is left sitting proud of the surface. Only after that is the paint clean enough to polish or protect. If fallout has been left long enough to etch, <a href="/paint-correction/">paint correction</a> is what removes the marks underneath, and we will tell you honestly which of the two you are looking at before quoting.',
